From 527f88cfe85fa3439180fb725d2e92c958df997f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sukrit Jaidee <45908411+SukritJaAIproject@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 06:02:37 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 29/30] fix(desktop): research panel opens any benchmark on its
 own policy arm; provenance notes

Follow-up to e74760ab, from an adversarial review of it:

- The panel opened on the benchmark's own arm only for ISO-2 + SLAC. Now that
  v4 has a replayed iso2 arm, an ISO-2-only v4 leaderboard matches the v4 grid
  ("same"). It opened on the projected SLAC arm with the AIAgent lower-bound
  note, instead of its own replayed arm. policyDefaultArm now uses any non-
  baseline policy arm the grid has. Baseline editions still open on
  + SLAC 600 ms. Covered by the ISO2_ONLY_BENCHMARK fixture (not an edition)
  and a relation test.
- Provenance: the two grids' iso2 arms were replayed on different trees. The
  2026-09-15 tree still had MultiAgent's V2G2-706 PreCharge vote, so its iso2
  MultiAgent cells differ on strict/reviewed. The difference is now documented
  and pinned. "Reproduces every 41ded2cd cell" now reads "every baseline and
  SLAC cell". For AIAgent's projected SLAC cells, only recall/FAR are lower
  bounds; its score moved 0.03 high on the ISO-2 records.
- The Snapshot edition's unmeasured tab keeps positive checks for its title
  and aria-describedby caption. The rewrite had left those unasserted.
- Stale comment "(v4 has no ISO 15118-2 replay)" fixed. desktop/README no
  longer calls the research panel identical in every edition.

304 tests pass; tsc is 130 total, 0 in fault-detection.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
